### 2. Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test)
**Ref:** Peruma et al., ESEC/FSE 2020 · testsmells.org  
**Test:** `ProcessOrder_CompletesWithoutError` (line 43)

```csharp
// ❌ SMELL — no assertion; passes even if ProcessOrder is completely broken
processor.ProcessOrder(order);
// method ends — MSTest reports "Passed" ✓
```

This test provides false confidence — the only thing it verifies is "no exception was thrown."

**Fix:** Assert on the expected side effects:
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void ProcessOrder_CompletesSuccessfully_SetsProcessedStatus()
{
    var processor = new OrderProcessor(_db, _email, _inventory);
    var order = new Order { Items = { new OrderItem("SKU-1", 1) } };

    var result = processor.ProcessOrder(order);

    Assert.AreEqual("StandardProcessed", result.Status);
    Assert.IsTrue(_db.WasOrderSaved(order.Id));
}
```

